 ### Surface Descendant Check
-A recursive function to determine if a node or any of its descendants are marked as active or contain a surface [S3, unofficial]. If the cell is a Leaf, it returns whether it has a sign change. If it is a Branch, it recursively checks if any of its children have a surface descendant. If it is Empty or Full, it returns false [S3, unofficial].
+A recursive function to determine if a node or any of its descendants are marked as active or contain a surface [S3, unofficial]. If the cell is a Leaf, it returns whether it has a sign change [S3, unofficial]. If it is a Branch, it recursively checks if any of its children have a surface descendant [S3, unofficial]. If it is Empty or Full, it returns false [S3, unofficial].
 
 ### Coarse Mesh Traversal via BVH
-Uses a Bounding Volume Hierarchy (BVH) built over the coarse tetrahedral mesh to efficiently locate the coarse element containing a sample point [S6, unofficial]. The BVH is built by inserting four triangular faces facing outside for every coarse element. Rays are traced using hit/miss functions; the hit function returns the hit point and coarse tetrahedron ID. Unlike element marching, this allows skipping coarse elements and varying refinement levels [S6, unofficial].
