 ### Two-Pass Hierarchy Traversal
-An optimization that splits traversal into two steps with a stopping depth in the first step. Step 1 traverses down to a specific depth relative to the leaves (e.g., depth=3). Step 2 traverses the remaining lower part for nodes identified in Step 1. At optimal stopping depth (3), it reduces time by 15% alone, and up to 30% with tile sharing. If stopping depth is 0, performance equals the direct implementation [S8].
